     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day, which is double the maximum labeled daily dose. The maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release in the US. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals**, which is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **500 mg to 1,000 mg twice daily**, which is the typical range.\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me and add a note about the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with that documented, though pharmacy will probably flag it. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
